  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.4.0.0\n\t\t\t- Released alongside NHSOneLondon.AuditAndMetrics.Clients 0.4.0.0, as the two packages always ship at the same version.\n\t\t\t- Breaking for every host that implements the storage port: ISecurityAudit has four new optional string properties. OriginIp is the IP address the request came from, IPv4 or IPv6, as text. ClientAppId (the calling app's client id, e.g. the Entra appid or azp claim), CallerType (free text such as \"Application\" or \"Delegated\") and TokenId (the access token's id, e.g. the Entra uti claim) describe the caller's token. Your SecurityAudit entity must implement all four, and your database needs four new columns and a migration: OriginIp nvarchar(45), ClientAppId nvarchar(255), CallerType nvarchar(255) and TokenId nvarchar(255), all nullable. Existing rows keep NULL.\n\t\t\t- The IAuditAndMetricStorageBroker methods are unchanged: they take the entity, which now carries the new values.\n\t\t\t- Upgrade guide: https://github.com/NHSISL/NHSOneLondon.AuditAndMetrics#upgrading-from-03x",
